Does finally always execute?

>> In ordinary control flow, it executes whether an exception occurs or not
    >> However, it is not an absolute guarantee: abrupt JVM termination, for example, can prevent it from running.

## Java automatically closes the BufferedReader when the try block exits.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.FileReader;
import java.io.IOException;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try (BufferedReader reader =
                 new BufferedReader(new FileReader("data.txt"))) {

            System.out.println(reader.readLine());

        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.out.println("Unable to read file");
        }
    }
}
